[quote="Melkhor"]

Gazelle form, and Environmental Allies was the big win for me.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Environmental Allies -- interesting. &nbsp;I&#39;ve not played the actual one-shot yet, but I&#39;ve played 5-6 practice matches on this setup, and pretty much abandoned Environmental Allies, because the few environment targets that actually do damage (as opposed to the Level and Structure cards) don&#39;t do much damage, and having Naturalist in Rhino Form to tank and avoid the +1 damage from his Nemesis seemed more useful. &nbsp; &nbsp;

&nbsp;

In my practice matches, Naturalist tended to get incapped. &nbsp;He would spend most of the game in Rhino Form, and I usually ended up in Indomitable Force right before it looked like Deadline was going to flip. &nbsp;Naturalist would take the 3-5HP AOE damage for everybody, then spend the rest of the game using his incap abilities to give AA multiple plays. &nbsp;AA usually had a good number of instruments/songs out by then, so giving AA one out-of-turn power usage usually resulted in the whole team getting a number of extra card plays/power usages. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

One thing I discovered was that with this group of heroes and Advanced Deadline, getting rid of his Deadline&#39;s Catastrophes usually doesn&#39;t help -- the 3 AOE damage per Catastrophe destroyed is a killer. &nbsp;

