While it&#39;s true that damage from environment targets isn&#39;t a huge risk on the platform, note that Environmental allies also offers an excellent degree of protection against Deadline&#39;s Calculated Orogenesis, as long as it flips a target (and there&#39;s a lot of those in the deck!), and as you mentioned yourself, with the pain it brings to take out Advanced Deadline&#39;s catastrophes, you&#39;re going to see a lot of those ;)

[quote="McBehrer"]

 KNYFE was the star damage dealer, but Argent Adept was pretty helpful too. 

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Anyone manage to get much of a contribution out of Expatriette? &nbsp; She starts the game with those tantalizing two Unloads, but I&#39;ve replayed the scenario a couple of times, and the most I ever got in play was the Assault Rifle, Pride, and a Submachine Gun. &nbsp;It made for an 8HP Unload hit (+1 damage to each gun for Predator&#39;s Eye), but that pales in comparison to what she can really do when she has a bunch of guns/ammo. &nbsp;One time I managed to get the Tac Shotgun in her hand, but she died before she could play it.

&nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

She was a consistent damage dealer for me. &nbsp;And helped reduce some damage for a round. &nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Yeah. &nbsp;I pulled out the Assault Rifle on her very first turn, and spent pretty much the entire game using it to do 1-3 2HP hits (sometimes more if I got lucky and grabbed an ammo or played Predator&#39;s Eye), but those two Unloads made me hope for more.....
